From f9b4e3b409f746893363baedc91e69643ff4188a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander <4418484+kuscher@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:30:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] feat(browser): the Android app on a PC can be the desktop
 app

On ChromeOS and in Android's desktop mode the Android app runs in a
resizable window with a keyboard and a mouse, like Collabora Office on
Windows, macOS and Linux, but the web UI only enables the desktop app's
behaviour (window.mode.isCODesktop(): the backstage File tab and starter
screen, the ruler by default, Ctrl+O and Ctrl+N, ...) for those three.

Let the Android app opt in: isCODesktop() is also true when the app's
COOLMessageHandler.isCODesktop() says so, asked once on first use like
isChromebook(). postMobileCall() returns the app's answer when the app
has a postMobileCall(), which the starter screen needs for
GETRECENTDOCS. The starter screen has no document and uses the
FakeWebSocket, as the desktop apps do. Ctrl+O and Ctrl+N map to Open and
the backstage's New tab for the Chromebook platform.

Some desktop features need things the Android app doesn't have, so they
stay off there: the presenter console and swapping monitors (a second
window), the welcome slideshow and "latest updates" (not packaged),
task workers (a file:// origin), and the Options dialog and AI set-up
(settings storage).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
